course: dictionary
lesson: 11142
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Wiggle can be an action you do with your toes, or a line that is not straight. Read the words around it to find which meaning is used. «Watch a cat with a toy mouse: its bottom wiggles, and then it shoots forward in one quick pounce.» The cat moves its bottom in small quick movements just before it jumps.
explain: Wiggle can also be a noun, «a wiggle», which is one small quick movement. A wiggly line is not straight: it goes from side to side in little waves. Ask yourself: is something moving, or is it a shape on the page?
explain: Some phrases mean something different from their separate words. «Wiggle room» means a little freedom to change something. «Get a wiggle on» means hurry up. When the words do not make sense one by one, look at the whole phrase, and check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence.
fact: To wiggle is to move with small quick movements from side to side or up and down.
fact: A wiggly line goes from side to side in little waves, so it is not straight.
fact: «Wiggle room» means a little freedom to change something; it is informal.
fact: «Get a wiggle on» means hurry up.
fact: «Wiggle out of» means to escape or avoid something.
exercise: «Watch a cat with a toy mouse: its bottom wiggles, and then it shoots forward in one quick pounce.» What does wiggles mean here? | Falls asleep | Makes a loud noise | Sits very still | *Moves with small quick movements
exercise: Mia says, «Could you get a wiggle on? We are late.» What does get a wiggle on mean? | Draw a wavy line | Dance very slowly | *Hurry up | Take a long nap
exercise: Ella drew a line that goes in little waves. What kind of line is it? | A straight line | A circle | *A wiggly line | A dot
test: «Our teacher gave us wiggle room to choose our own colours.» What does wiggle room mean here? | *A little freedom to change something | A room with no windows | A place to wiggle your toes | A lot of noise and mess
test: What does «wiggle out of» mean? | Dance to music | Hurry up | Move something back and forth carefully | *Escape or avoid something
exam: «The microwave makes the water inside the food wiggle.» What does wiggle mean in this sentence? | *Move with small quick movements | Stop moving completely | Turn into ice | Make a loud bang
